schema: doc/v1
epic: E-CRSCOPE
wu: E-CRSCOPE.W1
branch: wu/crscope/worktree-cache-slot
changes:
  - path: docs/decisions/workflow-gates.html
    tier: T2
    action: modified
    distills: "DEC-11's adopted-cut row, amended and not superseded, exactly as the epic plan's distillation section directs. The row now states the slot is per-worktree and lives at target/.gate0/ - `main` for the checkout that owns the repository, `worktrees/<name>` for a linked one - and records it as a correction to the DEC BY DRIFT: worktree provisioning post-dates DEC-11 and symlinks every worktree's target/ to one directory, so the original single key slot let each worktree evict the others' green and the adopted skip almost never fired. It also records why the slot root is a new path rather than the old file's: worktrees share target/debug/xtask, so a checkout still running the older binary writes .gate0-green as a plain file and a directory there would red every one of its gates. The soundness sentence is left untouched, because the soundness is untouched - the cache still stores the key it vouches for, never a verdict. A review round challenged the retained 'ephemeral and per-checkout' clause as contradicted; refuted on reading - in place that clause is the rationale for a local file rather than a synced git note, not a claim that slots were isolated."
  - path: docs/work/2026-09-06-crscope-w1-result.html
    tier: T3
    action: added
    distills: "The WU result: delivered against all four expected-result rows, with the headline claim MEASURED on the real six-worktree fleet rather than asserted (66.5s, 45.3s, 0.49s skip, 0.47s skip - the third being the run that was full before this WU). Two deviations with their reasons, chiefly that the slot root moved off the pre-slot file's path mid-WU because running the change in the real fleet - not in tempdirs - showed old and new binaries alternate on one target/. A four-round review section: twelve candidates, five verified and fixed, seven refuted with the evidence that refuted them. The evidence table, what went to T2, and three follow-ups - including the one this WU refuses to fix and hands to the epic close."
t2_synthesis:
  status: done
  what: "docs/decisions/workflow-gates.html carries this WU's permanent truth, in DEC-11's own row, which is the file that already owns gate-speed truth per the epic plan. No new DEC is minted: the epic plan reserves that for a configuration or effort rubric being adopted, and W1 adopts neither - it repairs a cut DEC-11 already adopted. No use case is touched: E-CRSCOPE serves no UC-* by construction, as its plan's use-case section records, and this WU changes no proxy, API or UI behaviour. The decisions index gains no row, because no record was added."
  code_change: "xtask/src/gate0.rs (the cache slot, and the public cached_green/record_green pair that expresses 'this worktree's green'), xtask/src/git.rs (worktree_slot/slot_of, deriving the slot from git's own git-dir and common-dir rather than the path's shape), xtask/tests/gate0_cache.rs (the two-worktree contract). None of it moves an observable contract, which is why no use case gains a row."
  infra_change: ".claude/skills/code-review/SKILL.md - the Gate 0 step named target/.gate0-green as 'a local per-checkout file'; it now names target/.gate0/<worktree> and states that worktrees share one target/ and never consume each other's green. Skill files are infrastructure and stay markdown per CLAUDE.md, so this carries no tier; it is listed because it is a rule-bearing description of the very gate this WU changed, and leaving it stale would have made the skill lie about where its own cache lives."
t1_note: "Untouched, and checked rather than assumed. workflow.html describes the gate contract - that a skip fires only when a recomputed key matches the cached one - and this WU does not alter it: what changed is which slot is consulted, not the rule. The epic plan states that if this turned out false it would be an escalation rather than a quiet edit; it did not turn out false."
